Z||000006||horseman||12-07-2000||07:52 PM||||Hey Guys,<P>What are the specs on the Lunati and Comp. cams? Are these all for the Duke? What about rocker arm clearances,springs and retainers,stud diam.'s and etc.?<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>charlie||||reg||5
Z||000007||rnoswal||12-07-2000||11:37 PM||||I went to the bone yards today in search of an intake and carb. I was looking for the postal vehicles and found a few 2.5s with a carbed intake manifold. I did notice though that the head was cast a little different. The intake ports were cast lower in the head and were larger than the EFI head on an 87 Fiero head that had been taken off. The exhaust was also different but still used the same type manifold, although it too was different in that it was a cast iron manifold. I am going to try this combination along with a cam and maybe some flat top pistons. It was amazing just how rough the castings were inside the intake and exhaust ports in these heads. I would love a v-6 but it sounds like too much has to be changed. Maybe I will come across a Fiero that already has a v-6, but until then....<BR>Anyone tried any of this stuff?<P>Russ||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||12-10-2000||01:43 AM||||Hey baldlobo can you send me those camshaft specification's I gave you dyno's on again?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
